text: ["({2/W} can be paid with any two mana or with {W}. This card's mana value is 10.)\\nOther Scarecrow creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever another Scarecrow enters the battlefield under your control, destroy target permanent.", "({W/P} can be paid with either {W} or 2 life.)\\nCreatures can't attack you or planeswalkers you control unless their controller pays {W/P} for each of those creatures.", 'Add {R}{R}{R}.', 'All Rats have fear.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a Rat: Create X 1/1 black Rat creature tokens, where X is the number of Rats you control.', 'All Sliver creatures get +1/+1.', 'All Slivers have "When this permanent enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact or enchantment."', 'Artifacts, creatures, and lands your opponents control enter the battlefield tapped.', "As Conspiracy enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nCreatures you control are the chosen type. The same is true for creature spells you control and creature cards you own that aren't on the battlefield.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nChoose target creature card in your graveyard. Return that card and the sacrificed card to the battlefield under your control at the beginning of your next upkeep. Exile Rescue from the Underworld.', "At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, that player chooses draw step, main phase, or combat phase. The player skips each instance of the chosen step or phase this turn.", "At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, that player loses 1 life for each card fewer than three in their hand.", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, that player puts the cards in their hand on the bottom of their library in any order, then draws that many cards.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, Form of the Dragon deals 5 damage to any target.\\nAt the beginning of each end step, your life total becomes 5.\\nCreatures without flying can't attack you.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, choose target opponent. This turn, that player can't cast spells or activate abilities and plays with their hand revealed. You may play lands and cast spells from that player's hand this turn.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may exchange control of target nonland permanent you control and target nonland permanent an opponent controls with an equal or lesser mana value.', "Aurelia's Fury deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of targets. Tap each creature dealt damage this way. Players dealt damage this way can't cast noncreature spells this turn.", 'Changeling (This card is every creature type.)\\nChampion a creature (When this enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you exile another creature you control. When this leaves the battlefield, that card returns to the battlefield.)\\nLifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', 'Changeling (This card is every creature type.)\\nTrample', "Choose one —\\n• Target player discards a card.\\n• Target creature gets +2/-1 until end of turn.\\n• Target creature gains swampwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", 'Chroma — When Springjack Shepherd enters the battlefield, create a 0/1 white Goat creature token for each white mana symbol in the mana costs of permanents you control.', 'Counter target spell or ability that targets a permanent you control.\\nThis spell costs {7} less to cast if it targets a spell or ability that targets a creature you control with power 7 or greater.', "Counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, put it on top of its owner's library instead of into that player's graveyard.", "Counter target spell. If the spell is countered this way, exile it with three time counters on it instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard. If it doesn't have suspend, it gains suspend. (At the beginning of its owner's upkeep, remove a time counter from that card. When the last is removed, the player plays it without paying its mana cost. If it's a creature, it has haste.)", "Creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nWhenever a creature enters the battlefield, untap all creatures.", 'Creatures you control get +0/+1.\\nMorph {1}{W} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Creatures you control have hexproof.\\nCreatures your opponents control lose hexproof and can't have or gain hexproof.", 'Cumulative upkeep—Add {R}. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', 'Defender, flying\\nCumulative upkeep—An opponent gains 1 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\nConspire (As you cast this spell, you may tap two untapped creatures you control that share a color with it. When you do, copy it and you may choose a new target for the copy.)', 'Destroy target artifact.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Destroy target enchantment.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Dethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nPay 3 life: Add {R}.', 'Discard your hand.', 'Dredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Each other Warrior creature you control enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has trample.', "Each player can't cast more than one spell each turn.", 'Each player draws three cards, then discards three cards at random.', 'Enchant instant card in a graveyard\\nWhenever you cast a sorcery spell, copy the enchanted instant card. You may cast the copy without paying its mana cost. If you do, exile the enchanted card and attach Spellweaver Volute to another instant card in a graveyard.', "Enchant player\\nAt the beginning of enchanted player's first upkeep each turn, that player gets an additional upkeep step after this step.", "Equipped creature has nonbasic landwalk. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a nonbasic land.)\\nEquip {2}", "First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nProtection from black (This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything black.)", "Flash\\nFlying, protection from blue\\nReturn a Forest you control to its owner's hand: Untap target creature. Activate only once each turn.", 'Flip a coin until you lose a flip or choose to stop flipping. If you lose a flip, Fiery Gambit has no effect. If you win one or more flips, Fiery Gambit deals 3 damage to target creature. If you win two or more flips, Fiery Gambit deals 6 damage to each opponent. If you win three or more flips, draw nine cards and untap all lands you control.', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Flying, haste\\nWhen Karrthus, Tyrant of Jund enters the battlefield, gain control of all Dragons, then untap all Dragons.\\nOther Dragon creatures you control have haste.', "Flying\\nCumulative upkeep—Gain control of a land you don't control. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nHerald of Leshrac gets +1/+1 for each land you control but don't own.\\nWhen Herald of Leshrac leaves the battlefield, each player gains control of each land they own that you control.", "Flying\\nDethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhenever Scourge of the Throne attacks for the first time each turn, if it's attacking the player with the most life or tied for most life, untap all attacking creatures. After this phase, there is an additional combat phase.", "Flying\\nOther Spirit creatures you control get +1/+1 and have hexproof. (They can't be the targets of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Chimney Imp dies, target opponent puts a card from their hand on top of their library.', "Flying\\nWhenever you cast a Spirit or Arcane spell, destroy all permanents with that spell's mana value.", "Flying\\nWither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nCreatures your opponents control with counters on them can't attack or block.", 'Flying\\nYou may cast Misthollow Griffin from exile.', 'Flying\\n{2}, {Q}: Add one mana of any color. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', 'Guerrilla Tactics deals 2 damage to any target.\\nWhen a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Guerrilla Tactics, Guerrilla Tactics deals 4 damage to any target.', 'Hornet Sting deals 1 damage to any target.', "If an opponent had three or more cards put into their graveyard from anywhere this turn, you may pay {0} rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nExile target player's graveyard.", 'If you would lose the game, instead shuffle your hand, your graveyard, and all permanents you own into your library, then draw seven cards and your life total becomes 20.', 'Imprint — When Knowledge Pool enters the battlefield, each player exiles the top three cards of their library.\\nWhenever a player casts a spell from their hand, that player exiles it. If the player does, they may cast a spell from among other cards exiled with Knowledge Pool without paying its mana cost.', "Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nBlighted Agent can't be blocked.", 'Kicker {R} (You may pay an additional {R} as you cast this spell.)\\nWhen Goblin Bushwhacker enters the battlefield, if it was kicked, creatures you control get +1/+0 and gain haste until end of turn.', "Lands you control are Plains.\\nNonland permanents you control are white. The same is true for spells you control and nonland cards you own that aren't on the battlefield.\\nYou may spend white mana as though it were mana of any color. You may spend other mana only as though it were colorless mana.", 'Lightning Storm deals X damage to any target, where X is 3 plus the number of charge counters on Lightning Storm.\\nDiscard a land card: Put two charge counters on Lightning Storm. You may choose a new target for it. Any player may activate this ability but only if Lightning Storm is on the stack.', "Maro's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.", 'Moonfolk offering (You may cast this card any time you could cast an instant by sacrificing a Moonfolk and paying the difference in mana costs between this and the sacrificed Moonfolk. Mana cost includes color.)\\nFlying\\n{1}: Put up to two land cards from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.', "Myojin of Life's Web enters the battlefield with a divinity counter on it if you cast it from your hand.\\nMyojin of Life's Web has indestructible as long as it has a divinity counter on it.\\nRemove a divinity counter from Myojin of Life's Web: Put any number of creature cards from your hand onto the battlefield.", "Noggle Bandit can't be blocked except by creatures with defender.", 'Other Snake creatures you control get +1/+0.\\nWhenever a Warrior you control deals combat damage to a creature, destroy that creature at end of combat.', 'Other blue creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{U}: Target artifact creature becomes blue until end of turn.\\nTap an untapped blue creature you control: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.', 'Other red creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther white creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, Balefire Liege deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, you gain 3 life.', 'Players play with the top card of their libraries revealed.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Lantern of Insight: Target player shuffles.', "Players play with their hands revealed.\\nIf a player would draw a card, they reveal it instead. Then any other player may pay 2 life. If a player does, put that card into its owner's graveyard. Otherwise, that player draws a card.", 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to creatures you control.', "Put target face-up exiled card into its owner's graveyard.", 'Return up to three target creature cards with mana value 1 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nForecast — {5}{W}, Reveal Proclamation of Rebirth from your hand: Return target creature card with mana value 1 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield. (Activate only during your upkeep and only once each turn.)', 'Sacrifice a creature: Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', 'Search your library for up to X basic land cards, where X is the number of lands you control, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Shroud (This enchantment can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\n{X}: Put X tower counters on Helix Pinnacle.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are 100 or more tower counters on Helix Pinnacle, you win the game.", 'Sliver creatures you control have "{T}: Add one mana of any color."', 'Spike Feeder enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Feeder: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Feeder: You gain 2 life.', "Target attacking creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature get -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent reveals cards from the top of their library until four land cards are revealed. That player puts all cards revealed this way into their graveyard.', 'The first spell you cast each turn has cascade. (When you cast your first spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.)', 'Trample\\nCumulative upkeep—Put a +1/+1 counter on a creature an opponent controls. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', "Trample\\nWhile you're searching your library, you may cast Panglacial Wurm from your library.", 'Triskelion enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Triskelion: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'When Flamekin Harbinger enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Elemental card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.', 'When Leveler enters the battlefield, exile all cards from your library.', 'When Ogre Gatecrasher enters the battlefield, destroy target creature with defender.', "When Witchbane Orb enters the battlefield, destroy all Curses attached to you.\\nYou have hexproof. (You can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control, including Aura spells.)", "When a player casts a spell or a creature attacks, exile Norin the Wary. Return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'When you have 30 or more life, flip Rune-Tail, Kitsune Ascendant.', 'Whenever Fungusaur is dealt damage, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever Yore-Tiller Nephilim attacks, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped and attacking.', 'Whenever a permanent enters the battlefield tapped and under your control, untap it.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player sacrifices a permanent unless they pay {1}.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a legendary spell, draw a card.', 'Will of the council — When Council Guardian enters the battlefield, starting with you, each player votes for blue, black, red, or green. Council Guardian gains protection from each color with the most votes or tied for most votes.', "Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever Stigma Lasher deals damage to a player, that player can't gain life for the rest of the game.", "You may exile two green cards from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nAllosaurus Rider's power and toughness are each equal to 1 plus the number of lands you control.", "You may have Rhox assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.\\n{2}{G}: Regenerate Rhox. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "You may pay {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nTrample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay 2 life. If you do, search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top.", 'You may reveal a multicolored card you own from outside the game and put it into your hand. Exile Glittering Wish.', 'Zombie spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\nZombie creatures you control get +2/+1.', "[0]: Reveal the top card of your library and put it into your hand. Sarkhan the Mad deals damage to himself equal to that card's mana value.\\n[−2]: Target creature's controller sacrifices it, then that player creates a 5/5 red Dragon creature token with flying.\\n[−4]: Each Dragon creature you control deals damage equal to its power to target player or planeswalker.", '{1}, {T}: End the turn. Activate only during your turn. (Exile all spells and abilities from the stack. Discard down to your maximum hand size. Damage wears off, and "this turn" and "until end of turn" effects end.)', '{1}, {T}: Untap target creature that has an activated ability with {T} in its cost.', '{1}{B}, {T}: Target opponent discards a card. Then if that player has no cards in hand, flip Nezumi Shortfang.', '{2}{G/U}, {Q}: Double the number of each kind of counter on target permanent. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', "{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Mindslaver: You control target player during that player's next turn. (You see all cards that player could see and make all decisions for the player.)", '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Blasting Station deals 1 damage to any target.\\nWhenever a creature enters the battlefield, you may untap Blasting Station.', "{T}: Add {B}.\\n{B}, {T}: Target legendary creature gains fear until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", '{T}: Add {C}.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{6}: Stalking Stones becomes a 3/3 Elemental artifact creature that's still a land. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G}{U}, {T}: You may cast spells this turn as though they had flash.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Put a charge counter on Mirrodin's Core.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Mirrodin's Core: Add one mana of any color.", '{T}: Add {R}.', '{T}: Add {U}.\\n{U}, {T}: Untap target legendary permanent.', '{T}: Target player mills a card. (They put the top card of their library into their graveyard.)\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Codex Shredder: Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: You may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.']
flavor: ['"After his death, monks spent ten years transcribing the tattoos from Reki\'s body and gathering stories from those who spoke with him. Thus the volume you hold was written."\\n—*The History of Kamigawa*', '"After years of study, I\'ve learned an important lesson: the relics we watch may be watching us back."\\n—Anowon, the Ruin Sage', '"Better for a doun to lose its cenn than its springjacks."', '"Everything comes with a price. Especially revolution."\\n—Grenzo, dungeon warden', '"I have a bad feeling about this."', '"I pity them, never knowing the pleasures of a single familiar form, but at least they find a noble shape at times."\\n—Desmera, perfect of Wren\'s Run', '"I see in their interconnectedness a strange embodiment of the natural order."\\n—Dionus, elvish archdruid', '"Keep your pace steady through the haze, lest you step on the heels of your future self or trip the self a moment behind you."\\n—Teferi', '"Let your heartbeat be the thunder in the valley. Let your swords be the lightning on the peaks."\\n—Lothar Lovisason, Balduvian chieftain', '"Planeswalking cannot be taught. Either you see the doors or you do not."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"Scouts of the Sakura Tribe spent two years wandering the forest to learn every leaf and tree. That knowledge was called upon during the Kami War to ensure the orochi\'s survival."\\n—*The History of Kamigawa*', '"Since the last sliver arrived, even our mightiest relics splinter into shards as soon as we bring them against the hive."\\n—Llanach, Skyshroud ranger', '"Step lightly and we might be able to use it as a bridge."\\n—Ib Halfheart, goblin tactician', '"The soul is only as eternal as I say it is."\\n—Sharuum the Hegemon', '"To a trained mind, the cold is but a momentary distraction."', '"Urabrask may suspect our surveillance, but he cannot stop it."\\n—Avaricta, Gitaxian sective', '"Why do bad things always come in threes?"\\n—Gisulf, expedition survivor', 'A popular game among ogres is to see how many revolutions a head can make before it pops off.', 'A single fear unleashes a torrent of nightmares.', 'All bow at its visitation—some in awe, some in honor, some in fear.', "As the muscle cords of the creature twitched, Hanna saw an unsettling unanimity in the others' rippling flesh. She didn't know what it meant, but she urged Sisay to keep the ship at a safe distance.", 'Centuries ago, Shizo was a verdant field of wildflowers. After 891 samurai died in a single battle on its grasses, it became a haunted moor.', 'Dead or alive, true leaders can inspire an entire army.', 'Despite its fearsome stature, it is as elusive as a shadow, circling round to stalk those who presume to hunt it.', 'Do the glowing trinkets show it the way home, or do they set a twisted path for someone else to follow?', 'Each eye sees a different possibility for tomorrow.', 'For some creatures, existing is only a whim.', 'Gjornersen entertained his followers by taking bets on which would move first—the drowsing land wurm or the frozen goblins.', 'Having conquered the Bastion of Suns, the Ota took its light for their own.', 'His assistants calculate the amount of the tribute. He measures out the punishment for delinquency.', 'In matters of life and death, he trusts his gut.', "In truth, her own faith was gone, trodden in Ulamog's wake. She pantomimed the blessing in the hope that it would inspire others to continue to struggle.", 'It has the strength of seven men. In fact, it used to be seven men.', 'It is best to conquer dragons before they hatch.\\n—Femeref adage', 'It is the soul of a philosopher who died of starvation contemplating the universe.', 'It shows not what you are but what you were.', "It was only then—to his infinite sorrow—that Gork realized hornets don't make honey.", "It wasn't really expected to fly. Then again, it wasn't expected to move, either.", "It's as solid as the club in its hand—and about as subtle.", "It's harvest time.", "It's much easier to list the places they *haven't* been.", 'Its students graduate the school and enter history.', 'Jariad burned the midnight oil, burned through scroll after scroll, and then burned down his laboratory.', "Man's best fungus.", 'Marrow-Gnawer united three nezumi gangs when he slew their leaders in a single night. Now they call him their first lord.', 'Mounted cinders circle the blasted peak at Kulrath, hunting the Extinguisher.', 'No one knows what she is watching, but she never takes her eyes off it.', 'No two see the same Maro.', 'Noggles believe that they were the first race ever to walk Shadowmoor. They don\'t "steal." They just take back what\'s rightfully theirs.', 'Once a century, the levelers rip through every corner of Mirrodin, obeying the commands of an unseen master.', 'One footstep among many is silent. One footstep alone is deafening.', "Persecuted alchemists fled deep into Kessig's wilds, seeking solitude to continue their ghoulish craft.", 'Rather than sheltering her young, the female fungusaur often injures her own offspring, thereby ensuring their rapid growth.', "Reminders of Memnarch's reign still skirr across Mirrodin, reminiscent of his form if not his power.", 'She wished for gold, but not for the strength to carry it.', "Some creatures are bound to the cold by Rimewind magic. Others seek it out, adapted by two thousand years of the Ice. The Boreal, where Heidar's frigid sway is strongest, is home to both.", 'Storm crow descending, winter unending. Storm crow departing, summer is starting.', "The Extinguisher's curse lasted long after her departure.", 'The Multiverse is filled with limitless power just waiting for someone to reach out and seize it.', "The book shrieks horribly until its cover is opened, granting the spirit inside a moment's rest from the painful stirrings of the book's contents.", 'The hound sniffed the air and let slip a low growl. General Takeno looked down at the faithful Isamaru and calmed him with a touch. "Alert the men. The kami are coming."', 'The myr are like rusted metal: gleaming purpose hidden by a thin disguise of debris.', 'The stones hark back to an age before civilization, when the living earth blessed all who trod its untamed wilds.', 'They are the masters of your mind.', 'Those who seek to escape her blades succeed only in dying on their stomachs.', 'When it awoke, the worms of the earth hissed in a chorus of beckoning.', 'When nothing remains, everything is equally possible.', 'Without a connection of mind and body, magic is just an idea stuck in the head, a word on the tip of a tongue.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Ash Wood', 'Bud Cook', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Scott', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Day', 'Donato Giancola', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Spalenka', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'Jason Felix', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'John Donahue', 'John Matson', 'John Stanko', 'Kev Walker', 'Liz Danforth', 'Luca Zontini', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael Komarck', 'Mike Bierek', 'Nils Hamm', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Scott Altmann', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stephen Tappin', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Stuart Griffin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Thomas Denmark', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'William Simpson', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
